{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-36-1","title":"Psalms 36:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The grievous estate of the wicked. 8 The excellency of God's mercy. 10 David prays for favour to God's children.</p>\n<p>A.M. cir. 3463. B.C. cir. 541. (Title.) A psalm.This Psalm is supposed by some to have been composed by David at the beginning of Saul's persecutions; but Calmet and others, on good grounds, are of opinion that it was written during the Babylonian captivity.</p>\n<p>servant. 18:1; 90:1; *titles 143:12; De 34:5; 2Ti 2:24; Tit 1:1; Jas 1:1; 2Pe 1:1; Jude 1:1 Re 1:1 The transgression.Or, rather, \"The speech of transgression to the wicked is within his heart: there is no fear of God before his eyes;\" for instead of {libbi,} \"my heart,\" four MSS., have {libbo,} \"his heart,\" which is also the reading of the LXX., Vulgate, Syriac, Arabic, Ethiopic, and Anglo-Saxon.</p>\n<p>1Sa 15:13,14; Pr 20:11; Mt 7:16-20; 12:33,34; Tit 1:16 no. 112:1; Ge 20:11; Pr 8:13; 16:6; Ec 12:13; Ro 3:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-2","title":"Psalms 36:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>For he. 10:3; 49:18; De 29:19; Jer 2:23,34,35; 17:9; Ho 12:7,8; Lu 10:29 Lu 16:14,15; Ro 7:9; 10:3 until, etc. Heb. to find his iniquity to hate. 1Sa 15:18-24; 1Ch 10:13,14; Ro 3:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-3","title":"Psalms 36:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>The words. 5:9; 12:2,3; 55:21; 58:3; 140:3; 1Sa 18:21; 19:6,7; 26:21 Mt 22:15-18,35 he hath. 125:5; 1Sa 11:6-13; 13:13,14; 15:26; 16:14; Zep 1:6; Heb 10:39 1Jo 2:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-4","title":"Psalms 36:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>deviseth. 38:12; 1Sa 19:11; Es 5:14; 6:4; Pr 4:16; Ho 7:6,7; Mic 2:1; Mt 27:1 Ac 23:12 mischief. or, vanity. setteth. Pr 24:23; Isa 65:2; Jer 6:16; 8:6; 9:2-9; Mic 6:8 abhorreth. 97:10; Job 15:16; Am 5:15; Ro 1:32; 12:9; Re 2:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-5","title":"Psalms 36:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>mercy. 52:1; 57:10; 103:11; 108:4; Isa 55:7-9 faithfulness. 89:2; 92:2; 100:5; Mt 24:35; Heb 6:18-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-6","title":"Psalms 36:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>righteousness. 71:19; 97:2; 145:17; Ge 18:25; De 32:4; Isa 45:19,21-24; Ro 3:25 great mountains. Heb. mountains of God. Ex 9:28; 1Sa 14:15; *margins judgments. 77:19; 92:5; Job 11:7-9; 37:23; Isa 40:28; Jer 12:1; Mt 11:25,26 Ro 11:33 thou. 104:14-35; 145:9; 147:9; Job 7:20; Jon 4:11; Mt 10:29,30; 1Ti 4:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-7","title":"Psalms 36:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>How. 31:19; 86:5,15; 145:7,8; Ex 34:6; Joh 3:16; 1Jo 3:1; 4:9,10 excellent. Heb. precious. 139:17; 1Pe 2:6,7; 2Pe 1:4 put their. 17:8; 57:1; 63:7; 91:4; Ru 2:12; Lu 13:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-8","title":"Psalms 36:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>abundantly. 16:11; 17:15; 63:5; 65:4; So 5:1; Isa 25:6; 55:1,2; Jer 31:12-14 Zec 9:17; Mt 5:6; Joh 7:37 satisfied. Heb. watered.{Yirweyun,} \"they shall be saturated,\" as a thirsty field by showers from heaven.</p>\n<p>Isa 58:11 and thou. 16:11; 46:4; Job 20:17; Isa 43:20; 48:21; Re 22:1-17 thy pleasures.Or, {adanacha,} \"thy pleasure,\" as four MSS., read; in which there is probably a reference to the garden of Eden, and the river that ran through, and watered it.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-9","title":"Psalms 36:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>For. Isa 12:3; Jer 2:13; Joh 4:10,14; 7:37-39; Re 21:6; 22:17 in thy. 27:1; Job 29:3; Pr 4:18; Isa 2:5; 60:1,2,19; Mal 4:2; Joh 1:8,9 Joh 8:12; 2Co 4:6; Jas 1:17; 1Pe 2:9; 1Jo 1:7; Re 21:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-10","title":"Psalms 36:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>continue. Heb. draw out at length. 103:17; Jer 31:3; Joh 15:9,10; 1Pe 1:5 that. 9:10; Jer 22:16; 24:7; Joh 17:3; Heb 8:11 and thy. 7:8-10; 18:24,25; 94:14,15; 97:10,11; 143:1,2; Isa 51:6-8 2Ti 4:7,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-11","title":"Psalms 36:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>foot. 10:2; 12:3-5; 119:51,69,85,122; 123:3,4; Job 40:11,12; Isa 51:23 Da 4:37 hand. 16:8; 17:8-14; 21:7,8; 62:6; 125:1-3; Ro 8:35-39</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-36-12","title":"Psalms 36:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":36,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":36,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>There. 9:16; 55:23; 58:10,11; 64:7-9; Jud 5:31; 2Th 1:8,9; Re 15:4; 19:1-6 shall. 1:5; 18:38; Jer 51:64</p>"}]}